    <main class="legal-content">
      <div class="summary">
        <h2>In short</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We collect your registration details and the profit-and-loss figures from the one accounting source you connect.</li>
          <li>We use them only to show you your dashboards. We do not sell your data, advertise to you, or track you with analytics.</li>
          <li>We only read reports from QuickBooks, Xero and Sage. We never create, change or delete anything in your accounting system.</li>
          <li>Your data is stored in South Africa. Email <a href="mailto:info@smart-builders.co.za">info@smart-builders.co.za</a> to see, correct or delete it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <section id="who-we-are">
        <h2><span class="num">1.</span>Who we are</h2>
        <p>Business Executive is a financial dashboard service operated by <strong>SmartBuilders</strong> ("we", "us", "our"). For the purposes of the Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (POPIA), SmartBuilders is the responsible party for the personal information described in this policy.</p>
        <p>This policy explains what information we collect when you use Business Executive, why we collect it, and the choices you have. It applies to the website and web application at bizexecdata.co.za.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-we-collect">
        <h2><span class="num">2.</span>What we collect</h2>

        <h3>Information you give us when you register</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>First name, surname, email address and telephone number</li>
          <li>Company name, business address and a description of your company's services</li>
          <li>Which accounting system you use</li>
          <li>A password, which we store only as a one-way hash, never as readable text</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Financial data from the source you connect</h3>
        <p>When you connect QuickBooks Online, Xero or Sage Business Cloud, we retrieve your <strong>profit-and-loss reports</strong>. That is up to three years of history when you first connect, and the most recent year each time you refresh. From those reports we store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Line items for revenue, cost of sales, expenses and other income, each with its category name, amount and month</li>
          <li>Monthly totals: sales, cost of sales, gross profit, operating expenses and net profit</li>
          <li>Identifiers for your company in that system, so your data can be matched to your account</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you upload an Excel or text income statement instead, we read the same kind of figures from the file. The file itself is processed in memory and is not kept.</p>

        <h3>Connection details</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>QuickBooks:</strong> the access and refresh tokens Intuit issues when you approve the connection, stored with your account so we can refresh your reports.</li>
          <li><strong>Xero:</strong> the access tokens Xero issues, held in your login session only.</li>
          <li><strong>Sage:</strong> Sage's API requires your Sage username and password on every request. We encrypt your password (AES-256) and hold it in your login session only, for as long as that session lasts. We never store it with your account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Technical information</h3>
        <p>Like most websites, our servers record each request: the page requested, your IP address, your browser's user-agent string and the time. Login and registration events also record the email address used. We use these logs to keep the service running and secure.</p>
        <p>We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking tools.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use">
        <h2><span class="num">3.</span>How we use it</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Information used</th><th>Lawful basis (POPIA s11)</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Creating and approving your account, and managing your licence</td><td>Registration details</td><td>Needed to provide the service you asked for</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Building your revenue, expense and profit dashboards</td><td>Financial data, connection details</td><td>Needed to provide the service you asked for</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Contacting you about your account, licence or a problem with the service</td><td>Name, email, telephone</td><td>Needed to provide the service; our legitimate interest in supporting you</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Keeping the service secure, preventing abuse and fixing faults</td><td>Technical information</td><td>Our legitimate interest in running a secure service</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Meeting legal obligations</td><td>Whatever the obligation requires</td><td>Compliance with the law</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>We do not use your information for marketing, and we do not make automated decisions about you.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="accounting-data">
        <h2><span class="num">4.</span>Your accounting data</h2>
        <p>Your financial data belongs to you. When you connect an accounting system:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>We only <strong>read</strong> profit-and-loss reports. We never create, edit or delete invoices, transactions, contacts or any other records.</li>
          <li>We use the data only to show dashboards to you and to the people you authorise on your account.</li>
          <li>We never sell it, rent it, or give it to anyone for their own use.</li>
          <li>You can revoke our access at any time from the connected apps settings in QuickBooks, Xero or Sage. Revoking access stops future updates. To have the data we already hold deleted as well, email us (see <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing">
        <h2><span class="num">5.</span>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>We share information only with the following, and only as far as they need it:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>, which hosts our servers and database. AWS acts as our operator and processes data only on our instructions.</li>
          <li><strong>Intuit (QuickBooks), Xero and Sage</strong>, but only the one you choose to connect, and only to request your reports on your behalf.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Fonts and jsDelivr</strong>, which supply fonts and chart libraries to your browser when pages load. They receive your IP address and browser details as part of that request, but none of your account or financial data.</li>
          <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, if the law requires us to disclose information, or to protect our rights or someone's safety.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="storage">
        <h2><span class="num">6.</span>Where it is stored</h2>
        <p>Our servers, database and logs are hosted by Amazon Web Services in its Cape Town region, in South Africa.</p>
        <p>QuickBooks, Xero and Sage are operated from outside South Africa, so your financial data travels from their servers to ours when we fetch your reports. You have already chosen to keep that data with them; we do not send your data to them or to any other country.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2><span class="num">7.</span>How we protect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>All traffic between your browser and our service is encrypted with TLS (HTTPS).</li>
          <li>Our database is encrypted at rest, has no public internet access, and accepts only encrypted connections from our application.</li>
          <li>Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes. Sage passwords are encrypted and never stored with your account.</li>
          <li>Accounts must be approved by an administrator before they can sign in, and repeated failed logins are rate-limited.</li>
          <li>Each user's dashboards return only that user's data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal information, we will notify you and the Information Regulator as POPIA requires.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <h2><span class="num">8.</span>How long we keep it</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Information</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Account and financial data</td><td>While your account is active. If you close your account, we delete it within 30 days, unless the law requires us to keep it longer.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>QuickBooks connection tokens</td><td>Until you disconnect, your account is closed, or Intuit revokes them</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Xero tokens and encrypted Sage password</td><td>For the length of your login session (at most 24 hours)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Server logs</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Database backups</td><td>7 days, after which deleted data disappears from backups too</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <h2><span class="num">9.</span>Cookies</h2>
        <p>We set a single, essential cookie that keeps you signed in. It expires after 24 hours and cannot be used to track you on other websites. We also save in your browser whether you prefer the sidebar collapsed, and the dashboard filters you last selected. None of this is sent to anyone else.</p>
        <p>We do not use advertising or analytics cookies, so there is nothing to opt out of.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <h2><span class="num">10.</span>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under POPIA you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask whether we hold personal information about you, and receive a copy of it</li>
          <li>Ask us to correct or update information that is inaccurate or out of date</li>
          <li>Ask us to delete your information, or to close your account</li>
          <li>Object to us processing your information on the basis of our legitimate interests</li>
          <li>Complain to the Information Regulator</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To make a request, email <a href="mailto:info@smart-builders.co.za">info@smart-builders.co.za</a> from the email address on your account. We will respond within 30 days. We may ask you to confirm your identity first.</p>
        <p>If you are unhappy with how we handle your information, please contact us first so we can try to fix it. You can also complain to the <strong>Information Regulator (South Africa)</strong> at <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener">inforegulator.org.za</a>, or by email at <a href="mailto:POPIAComplaints@inforegulator.org.za">POPIAComplaints@inforegulator.org.za</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2><span class="num">11.</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page. If a change significantly affects how we use your information, we will tell you before it takes effect.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2><span class="num">12.</span>Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy or your information go to our Information Officer:</p>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <div><span>Company</span>SmartBuilders</div>
          <div><span>Email</span><a href="mailto:info@smart-builders.co.za">info@smart-builders.co.za</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
